From 4da3ac15154c2f1923652ccbcbfa596f466b1712 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chiro <chiro2001@163.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 20:43:24 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 139/250] feat(sve256): execute iota/compare and
 broadcast/where natively

W8B B2 closes the four position/control and data-movement fallback
classes on cpu.aarch64.sve256:

- runner protocol v5 adds compact control descriptors: iota (PXIO) and
  compare (PXCP) are executed inside the AArch64 ELF, so the Python
  iota_values()/compare_values() host-reference boundary is gone.
- broadcast (PXBD) and where (PXWH) send raw storage plus output-rank
  broadcast strides; the ELF performs every source lookup.  The artifact
  now advertises host_preexpanded_operations=[] instead of
  ["broadcast","where"] and position_control_fallback="native".
- SVE256_LOWERING_VERSION 6 -> 7 so v4/v5/v6 artifacts and the old
  preexpanded wire contract fail closed instead of being reinterpreted.
- focused QEMU differential covers non-multiple-of-8 tails, NaN/Inf,
  empty shapes, scalar/rank-delta broadcast, all compare predicates and
  int32/int64/uint8/uint64/bool/bf16/float32 dtypes.
